course: dictionary
lesson: 4845
title: Hyenas: more than villains
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: A hyena is a wild animal from Africa and parts of Asia. It looks a bit like a dog, but it is not a dog. Scientists say it is more closely related to cats and mongooses.
explain: Cartoons often show hyenas as sneaky villains. Read the clue: «the hyena is not just a sneaky thief» tells you the writer thinks that picture is unfair. When a text says something is "not just" one thing, it is often correcting a wrong idea.
explain: A sound can have a meaning too. «A spotted hyena's giggle usually means it is nervous, excited or frustrated, not happy.» The words "not happy" are the clue: the giggle is not a sign of joy.
fact: A hyena is a wild animal from Africa and parts of Asia.
fact: Spotted hyenas have some of the strongest bites of any mammal, and they can crush bones.
fact: Hyenas hunt in groups, and they also eat what other animals leave behind.
fact: Spotted hyenas hunt most of their own food.
fact: Hyenas are more closely related to cats and mongooses than to dogs.
exercise: «Spotted hyenas have some of the strongest bites of any mammal.» What does this tell us about hyenas? | *They can crush bones with their jaws | They bite only fruit | They cannot eat meat at all | They are the weakest animals in Africa
exercise: «The hyena is not just a sneaky thief.» What does this sentence tell us the writer thinks? | Hyenas are thieves who steal everything | Hyenas are the best hunters that never eat leftovers | Hyenas live high up in trees | *The cartoon idea of hyenas is unfair
exercise: «A spotted hyena's giggle usually means it is nervous, excited or frustrated, not happy.» What does a giggle usually mean? | The hyena is hungry for fruit | *The hyena is nervous, excited or frustrated | The hyena is asleep | The hyena is happy and playing
test: Hyenas eat what other animals leave behind. What is the word for finding and eating food that other animals have left? | *Scavenging | Swimming | Hunting alone | Growing fruit
test: «Spotted hyenas live in clans led by females.» What is a clan? | *A group of animals that live together | Ahole in the ground | A kind of bone | A type of lion
exam: Which fact about hyenas is true? | Hyenas live only in the Arctic | Hyenas are a kind of dinosaur | Hyenas cannot hunt at all | *Hyenas are more closely related to cats than to dogs
